WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
In 2023, women working full time in the US

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.730
had median weekly
earnings of 1,005 dollars.

3
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:11.980
For men, the median was 1,202 dollars.

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:16.180
Women earned 83.6 percent of men's median.

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.830
But a gap is not all discrimination.

6
00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:22.070
Hours, jobs and career breaks differ too.

7
00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.030
So if two workers are equally productive,

8
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.010
how can one still end up paid less?

9
00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll see
how researchers sent nearly

10
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.710
5,000 résumés that
differed only in the name.

11
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.030
Then you'll use a graph
lab to measure what

12
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.710
prejudice costs one group of workers.

13
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain how equally
productive workers can end up paid less.
